{"timestamp":"2026-09-23T23:35:15.644Z","ordinal":89819,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_096c433c75860d41016ab4623312348191b3f04a579ff427ad","status":"completed","call_id":"call_nBxjkzxtBTtkVIT57YuFkYUC","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,220p' /Users/cooper/Projects/site/docs/architecture/package-ownership.md\",max_output_tokens:3200});text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0d09d-47a5-7db3-b179-80b63f2ed88a","create_time":1790206507.290374}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-23T23:35:15.714Z","ordinal":89820,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"019f3c64-2576-70c2-90c0-e6b212f79ee1","turn_id":"01a0d09d-47a5-7db3-b179-80b63f2ed88a","session_id":"019f3c64-2576-70c2-90c0-e6b212f79ee1","root_turn_id":"01a0d09d-47a5-7db3-b179-80b63f2ed88a","response_id":"resp_096c433c75860d41016ab4622b23048191b1c036769a0a8c8f","usage":{"input_tokens":95127,"cached_input_tokens":92544,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":329,"reasoning_output_tokens":272,"total_tokens":95456},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2584839,"cached_input_tokens":2505088,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":4683,"reasoning_output_tokens":839,"total_tokens":2589522},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":51046981,"cached_input_tokens":50204288,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":93289,"reasoning_output_tokens":39743,"total_tokens":51140270}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-23T23:35:15.741Z","ordinal":89821,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019f3c64-2576-70c2-90c0-e6b212f79ee1","turn_id":"01a0d09d-47a5-7db3-b179-80b63f2ed88a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-92a3b4fc-0a2e-41f7-b9bb-936411b69ca0","process_id":"70653","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,220p' /Users/cooper/Projects/site/docs/architecture/package-ownership.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/Projects/bundjil","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,220p' /Users/cooper/Projects/site/docs/architecture/package-ownership.md","name":"package-ownership.md","path":"/Users/cooper/Projects/site/docs/architecture/package-ownership.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"---\ndocument_type: architecture\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: site-architecture-owner\nlast_reviewed: 2026-09-14\nreview_trigger: package ownership, exports, app composition or generated source boundary change\n---\n\n# Package Ownership\n\nThis repo uses a compact workspace. Keep docs and imports aligned to the\npackages that actually exist.\n\n## `apps/web`\n\nThe deployable TanStack Start app owns:\n\n- file routes in `apps/web/src/routes`\n- app-only components in `apps/web/src/components`\n- server and client runtime composition in `apps/web/src/lib`\n- server-only metric/proof Schemas, instruments, closed proof-log program,\n  OTLP Layer, and deployment adapter in `apps/web/src/lib/observability` and\n  `apps/web/src/lib/deployment`\n- build-time Vite adapters under `apps/web/src/lib/build/vite`\n- Vite, fumadocs-mdx, Tailwind, and image tooling configuration\n- the app-owned static page collection, Effect validation and representations\n  under `apps/web/src/lib/page-content`; `apps/web/source.config.ts` combines\n  page and post collections without generating package indexes\n- generated OG image assets and scripts\n\nIt may import from `@packages/aeo`, `@packages/effect-start`,\n`@packages/http-api`, `@packages/mcp`, `@packages/og`, `@packages/posts`,\n`@packages/infrastructure`, `@packages/route-verification`, `@packages/rpc`,\n`@packages/seo`, and `@packages/ui`. It should not import from\n`@packages/scripts` at application runtime.\n\nCloudflare host binding access stays in the app deployment adapter. The root\nAlchemy stack owns the Redacted Secrets Store payload, while the app owns its\nSchema decode, runtime-config service, request metrics and metrics transport.\nNeither reusable package nor client runtime may import `cloudflare:workers`,\nAxiom credentials, or unstable OTLP modules.\n\nField definitions must live with the package that owns their meaning. Consumers\nreuse exported schemas, branded types, or derived projections instead of\nredeclaring local `id: string`, `slug: string`, status, or metadata shapes.\n\n## `@packages/infrastructure`\n\nInfrastructure owns the source-run Alchemy resource graph and its shared\nconfiguration contracts:\n\n- Cloudflare Website, route and stage-output policy;\n- Axiom dataset, token, dashboard and token-qualification declarations;\n- the observability export plan and stage Schema;\n- deployment identity and Worker metrics-config Schemas;\n- provider egress for the Redacted metrics secret; and\n- the site graph composed by the root Alchemy entrypoint.\n\nThe package exposes only `./stack`, `./observability`, `./schemas` and\n`./dashboards`. The root Alchemy files, web app and read-only dashboard tool\nmust use those exports. They must not import package `src/**` paths. The\npackage is source-only because Alchemy and Bun execute the TypeScript graph\ndirectly; its tests prove local graph policy, not provider state.\n\n## `@packages/effect-start`\n\nEffect Start owns reusable TanStack Start adapters for Effect programs:\n\n- request middleware adapters that run Effect HTTP programs through a provided\n  `ManagedRuntime`\n- Web `Request` to `HttpServerRequest` provisioning\n- `HttpServerResponse` to Web `Response` conversion, including HEAD\n  `withoutBody` handling\n- TanStack `next()` Promise bridging at the framework boundary\n\nIt must stay generic. It must not import `apps/web`, app route modules,\n`@packages/aeo`, `@packages/posts`, React components, or site runtime\ncomposition. Applications own the concrete runtime, Markdown sibling registry,\ndomain program, and any server-only import fence needed by their bundler. In\nthis app, that fence is limited to the Markdown sibling middleware because\nTanStack production import protection rejects direct `runtime.server` imports\nthrough `src/start.ts`.\n\n## `@packages/posts`\n\nPosts owns content discovery and the post service contract:\n\n- frontmatter and post schemas\n- the branded `PostSlug` identity and its source/HTTP API/RPC/route ingress\n  contract\n- post errors\n- `PostsService` and live layers\n- fumadocs-mdx source config\n- generated `.source/*` integration\n- client and server post loaders\n\nThe package source config is the sole generator of `packages/posts/.source`.\nApp Fumadocs composition uses `index: false`; generated package files must not\nimport app collections or compete with a second index writer.\n\nThis package is source-only by design. Its exports point at TypeScript source\nbecause `.source/*` uses Vite features that a plain `tsc` dist cannot preserve.\n\n## `@packages/http-api`\n\nHTTP API owns the cacheable public post transport:\n\n- `SiteHttpApi`, its posts group, and HTTP request envelopes;\n- generated-client type and service ownership without a handwritten client\n  interface;\n- handlers that delegate directly to `PostsService`;\n- browser Fetch and parameterized in-process client layers;\n- the server router layer and generated-client integration fixtures.\n\nIt reuses posts-owned schemas, branded `PostSlug`, projections, and tagged\nerrors. It must not import concrete posts Vite, Bun, Cloudflare, memory, or live\nlayers; app runtime composition supplies `PostsService`. It must not import or\nderive contracts from `@packages/rpc`. `SiteHttpApi` is public-read-only while\nthe app's successful-GET middleware is scoped to its entire router; private or\npersonalized groups require a separately composed cache boundary.\n\n## `@packages/rpc`\n\nRPC owns the retained compatibility transport:\n\n- `SiteRpcGroup`, its operation definitions, and RPC envelopes;\n- the typed client service, browser and in-process transports, handlers, and\n  test fixtures;\n- the `/rpc` HTTP layer composed by the app.\n\nRPC handlers delegate to the same published-only `PostsService` operations as\nthe HTTP API, but the transport definitions remain independent. Public post\nroute loaders use `@packages/http-api`; RPC remains mounted and verified as a\nseparate `no-store` contract.\n\n## `@packages/mcp`\n\nMCP owns the concrete public, read-only posts resource transport:\n\n- `SiteMcpHttp` and package-owned policy/URI/slug Schemas at the contract root;\n- `makeSiteMcpHttpLive(identity)` at `./live`, requiring `PostsService`;\n- the scoped memory-composed custom fetch at `./testing`; and\n- the private official SDK `McpServer.server` seam, Web Standard transport,\n  request Schemas, selected Cloudflare validator, resource encoding, HTTP\n  policy, and lifecycle. The selected validator, emitted production import /\n  constructor graph, and direct pinned-workerd execution together own the\n  Cloudflare-safe local bundle gate; retained unselected Ajv/default-provider\n  and Zod dynamic-code markers are not failures by themselves. The package\n  owns a bounded shutdown policy and instrumented release proof, but does not\n  own an MCP envelope parser or bundle transform.\n\nIt may depend on `@packages/posts` and `@packages/seo`. It must not import\n`apps/web`, TanStack Start, provider APIs, concrete post sources, app\nobservability, or another site transport. SDK types, constructors, errors, and\nresult shapes are not public exports. The app owns identity values, source\nselection, runtime composition, observability, and `/mcp` mounting.\n\nThe app additionally owns the local emitted-Worker proof runtime and its one\nco-located Web/Schema boundary. Those files may observe `@packages/mcp` only\nthrough the built app graph; they do not widen the contract-only root,\n`./live`, or `./testing` exports and do not create a reusable Fetch or SDK\nabstraction.\n\n## `@packages/seo`\n\nSEO owns reusable metadata contracts:\n\n- site identity, canonical URL/path, SEO text, author, image, Open Graph, and\n  Twitter schemas\n- route SEO page definitions and generated route head descriptors\n- generic `ArticleSeoData` without post slug, tags, source paths, or route\n  policy\n- schema-owned route breadcrumb and navigation labels\n- JSON-LD schemas and builders for site, person, page, blog, blog post, and\n  breadcrumbs\n\nIt must not import `apps/web`, TanStack Start routes, React components,\nfumadocs loaders, or `@packages/posts`. Canonical post metadata may be\nstructurally passed as `ArticleSeoData`, while the app supplies the canonical\npath separately. SEO must not own a post-facing DTO mirror.\n\n## `@packages/aeo`\n\nAEO owns reusable machine-readable contracts:\n\n- Accept-only negotiation schemas and tagged decision values\n- Markdown representation schemas\n- robots, sitemap, `llms.txt`, and `llms-full.txt` schemas/renderers\n- immutable `AeoCatalogSnapshot`, `AeoSiteConfiguration`, `AeoCatalog` service\n  contracts, machine programs/renderers, and memory layers for tests\n- Effect HTTP response programs for machine routes\n- redirect-only Markdown sibling negotiation contracts and program factories\n- bounded RFC 9264 API Catalog schemas/programs and the closed registered\n  `api-catalog`/`alternate` RFC 8288 Link Schema, encoder, parser, merge, order,\n  and exact-deduplication operation\n\nIt must not import `apps/web`, TanStack Start routes, React components,\nfumadocs loaders, or `@packages/posts`. Apps compose post-backed and\nroute-backed catalog derivation and provide its snapshot to `AeoCatalog`. Apps also own the\nconcrete Markdown sibling route registry and all route-owned `.md` rendering.\nThe Site app also owns the exact three-root API Catalog value, literal\n`/.well-known/api-catalog` route, and Link applicability. The package never\nimports the Site transport inventory or decides which app responses advertise\nit.\n\n## `@packages/og`\n\nOG owns reusable image-rendering infrastructure:\n\n- schema-backed render options and rendered image contracts\n- tagged renderer and Takumi client errors\n- `OgRenderer` and `TakumiClient` service contracts\n- dependency-requiring `OgRendererTakumiLayer`\n- composed `OgRendererNativeLive` backed by `TakumiClientLive`\n- mock renderer plus test-supplied `TakumiClient` layers\n\nIt must stay generic. It must not import SEO catalogs, `apps/web`,\n`@packages/posts`, TanStack Start routes, or\nsite-specific React components. Apps provide render data, assets, components,\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"---\ndocument_type: architecture\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: site-architecture-owner\nlast_reviewed: 2026-09-14\nreview_trigger: package ownership, exports, app composition or generated source boundary change\n---\n\n# Package Ownership\n\nThis repo uses a compact workspace. Keep docs and imports aligned to the\npackages that actually exist.\n\n## `apps/web`\n\nThe deployable TanStack Start app owns:\n\n- file routes in `apps/web/src/routes`\n- app-only components in `apps/web/src/components`\n- server and client runtime composition in `apps/web/src/lib`\n- server-only metric/proof Schemas, instruments, closed proof-log program,\n  OTLP Layer, and deployment adapter in `apps/web/src/lib/observability` and\n  `apps/web/src/lib/deployment`\n- build-time Vite adapters under `apps/web/src/lib/build/vite`\n- Vite, fumadocs-mdx, Tailwind, and image tooling configuration\n- the app-owned static page collection, Effect validation and representations\n  under `apps/web/src/lib/page-content`; `apps/web/source.config.ts` combines\n  page and post collections without generating package indexes\n- generated OG image assets and scripts\n\nIt may import from `@packages/aeo`, `@packages/effect-start`,\n`@packages/http-api`, `@packages/mcp`, `@packages/og`, `@packages/posts`,\n`@packages/infrastructure`, `@packages/route-verification`, `@packages/rpc`,\n`@packages/seo`, and `@packages/ui`. It should not import from\n`@packages/scripts` at application runtime.\n\nCloudflare host binding access stays in the app deployment adapter. The root\nAlchemy stack owns the Redacted Secrets Store payload, while the app owns its\nSchema decode, runtime-config service, request metrics and metrics transport.\nNeither reusable package nor client runtime may import `cloudflare:workers`,\nAxiom credentials, or unstable OTLP modules.\n\nField definitions must live with the package that owns their meaning. Consumers\nreuse exported schemas, branded types, or derived projections instead of\nredeclaring local `id: string`, `slug: string`, status, or metadata shapes.\n\n## `@packages/infrastructure`\n\nInfrastructure owns the source-run Alchemy resource graph and its shared\nconfiguration contracts:\n\n- Cloudflare Website, route and stage-output policy;\n- Axiom dataset, token, dashboard and token-qualification declarations;\n- the observability export plan and stage Schema;\n- deployment identity and Worker metrics-config Schemas;\n- provider egress for the Redacted metrics secret; and\n- the site graph composed by the root Alchemy entrypoint.\n\nThe package exposes only `./stack`, `./observability`, `./schemas` and\n`./dashboards`. The root Alchemy files, web app and read-only dashboard tool\nmust use those exports. They must not import package `src/**` paths. The\npackage is source-only because Alchemy and Bun execute the TypeScript graph\ndirectly; its tests prove local graph policy, not provider state.\n\n## `@packages/effect-start`\n\nEffect Start owns reusable TanStack Start adapters for Effect programs:\n\n- request middleware adapters that run Effect HTTP programs through a provided\n  `ManagedRuntime`\n- Web `Request` to `HttpServerRequest` provisioning\n- `HttpServerResponse` to Web `Response` conversion, including HEAD\n  `withoutBody` handling\n- TanStack `next()` Promise bridging at the framework boundary\n\nIt must stay generic. It must not import `apps/web`, app route modules,\n`@packages/aeo`, `@packages/posts`, React components, or site runtime\ncomposition. Applications own the concrete runtime, Markdown sibling registry,\ndomain program, and any server-only import fence needed by their bundler. In\nthis app, that fence is limited to the Markdown sibling middleware because\nTanStack production import protection rejects direct `runtime.server` imports\nthrough `src/start.ts`.\n\n## `@packages/posts`\n\nPosts owns content discovery and the post service contract:\n\n- frontmatter and post schemas\n- the branded `PostSlug` identity and its source/HTTP API/RPC/route ingress\n  contract\n- post errors\n- `PostsService` and live layers\n- fumadocs-mdx source config\n- generated `.source/*` integration\n- client and server post loaders\n\nThe package source config is the sole generator of `packages/posts/.source`.\nApp Fumadocs composition uses `index: false`; generated package files must not\nimport app collections or compete with a second index writer.\n\nThis package is source-only by design. Its exports point at TypeScript source\nbecause `.source/*` uses Vite features that a plain `tsc` dist cannot preserve.\n\n## `@packages/http-api`\n\nHTTP API owns the cacheable public post transport:\n\n- `SiteHttpApi`, its posts group, and HTTP request envelopes;\n- generated-client type and service ownership without a handwritten client\n  interface;\n- handlers that delegate directly to `PostsService`;\n- browser Fetch and parameterized in-process client layers;\n- the server router layer and generated-client integration fixtures.\n\nIt reuses posts-owned schemas, branded `PostSlug`, projections, and tagged\nerrors. It must not import concrete posts Vite, Bun, Cloudflare, memory, or live\nlayers; app runtime composition supplies `PostsService`. It must not import or\nderive contracts from `@packages/rpc`. `SiteHttpApi` is public-read-only while\nthe app's successful-GET middleware is scoped to its entire router; private or\npersonalized groups require a separately composed cache boundary.\n\n## `@packages/rpc`\n\nRPC owns the retained compatibility transport:\n\n- `SiteRpcGroup`, its operation definitions, and RPC envelopes;\n- the typed client service, browser and in-process transports, handlers, and\n  test fixtures;\n- the `/rpc` HTTP layer composed by the app.\n\nRPC handlers delegate to the same published-only `PostsService` operations as\nthe HTTP API, but the transport definitions remain independent. Public post\nroute loaders use `@packages/http-api`; RPC remains mounted and verified as a\nseparate `no-store` contract.\n\n## `@packages/mcp`\n\nMCP owns the concrete public, read-only posts resource transport:\n\n- `SiteMcpHttp` and package-owned policy/URI/slug Schemas at the contract root;\n- `makeSiteMcpHttpLive(identity)` at `./live`, requiring `PostsService`;\n- the scoped memory-composed custom fetch at `./testing`; and\n- the private official SDK `McpServer.server` seam, Web Standard transport,\n  request Schemas, selected Cloudflare validator, resource encoding, HTTP\n  policy, and lifecycle. The selected validator, emitted production import /\n  constructor graph, and direct pinned-workerd execution together own the\n  Cloudflare-safe local bundle gate; retained unselected Ajv/default-provider\n  and Zod dynamic-code markers are not failures by themselves. The package\n  owns a bounded shutdown policy and instrumented release proof, but does not\n  own an MCP envelope parser or bundle transform.\n\nIt may depend on `@packages/posts` and `@packages/seo`. It must not import\n`apps/web`, TanStack Start, provider APIs, concrete post sources, app\nobservability, or another site transport. SDK types, constructors, errors, and\nresult shapes are not public exports. The app owns identity values, source\nselection, runtime composition, observability, and `/mcp` mounting.\n\nThe app additionally owns the local emitted-Worker proof runtime and its one\nco-located Web/Schema boundary. Those files may observe `@packages/mcp` only\nthrough the built app graph; they do not widen the contract-only root,\n`./live`, or `./testing` exports and do not create a reusable Fetch or SDK\nabstraction.\n\n## `@packages/seo`\n\nSEO owns reusable metadata contracts:\n\n- site identity, canonical URL/path, SEO text, author, image, Open Graph, and\n  Twitter schemas\n- route SEO page definitions and generated route head descriptors\n- generic `ArticleSeoData` without post slug, tags, source paths, or route\n  policy\n- schema-owned route breadcrumb and navigation labels\n- JSON-LD schemas and builders for site, person, page, blog, blog post, and\n  breadcrumbs\n\nIt must not import `apps/web`, TanStack Start routes, React components,\nfumadocs loaders, or `@packages/posts`. Canonical post metadata may be\nstructurally passed as `ArticleSeoData`, while the app supplies the canonical\npath separately. SEO must not own a post-facing DTO mirror.\n\n## `@packages/aeo`\n\nAEO owns reusable machine-readable contracts:\n\n- Accept-only negotiation schemas and tagged decision values\n- Markdown representation schemas\n- robots, sitemap, `llms.txt`, and `llms-full.txt` schemas/renderers\n- immutable `AeoCatalogSnapshot`, `AeoSiteConfiguration`, `AeoCatalog` service\n  contracts, machine programs/renderers, and memory layers for tests\n- Effect HTTP response programs for machine routes\n- redirect-only Markdown sibling negotiation contracts and program factories\n- bounded RFC 9264 API Catalog schemas/programs and the closed registered\n  `api-catalog`/`alternate` RFC 8288 Link Schema, encoder, parser, merge, order,\n  and exact-deduplication operation\n\nIt must not import `apps/web`, TanStack Start routes, React components,\nfumadocs loaders, or `@packages/posts`. Apps compose post-backed and\nroute-backed catalog derivation and provide its snapshot to `AeoCatalog`. Apps also own the\nconcrete Markdown sibling route registry and all route-owned `.md` rendering.\nThe Site app also owns the exact three-root API Catalog value, literal\n`/.well-known/api-catalog` route, and Link applicability. The package never\nimports the Site transport inventory or decides which app responses advertise\nit.\n\n## `@packages/og`\n\nOG owns reusable image-rendering infrastructure:\n\n- schema-backed render options and rendered image contracts\n- tagged renderer and Takumi client errors\n- `OgRenderer` and `TakumiClient` service contracts\n- dependency-requiring `OgRendererTakumiLayer`\n- composed `OgRendererNativeLive` backed by `TakumiClientLive`\n- mock renderer plus test-supplied `TakumiClient` layers\n\nIt must stay generic. It must not import SEO catalogs, `apps/web`,\n`@packages/posts`, TanStack Start routes, or\nsite-specific React components. Apps provide render data, assets, components,\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":9042},"formatted_output":"---\ndocument_type: architecture\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: site-architecture-owner\nlast_reviewed: 2026-09-14\nreview_trigger: package ownership, exports, app composition or generated source boundary change\n---\n\n# Package Ownership\n\nThis repo uses a compact workspace. Keep docs and imports aligned to the\npackages that actually exist.\n\n## `apps/web`\n\nThe deployable TanStack Start app owns:\n\n- file routes in `apps/web/src/routes`\n- app-only components in `apps/web/src/components`\n- server and client runtime composition in `apps/web/src/lib`\n- server-only metric/proof Schemas, instruments, closed proof-log progr