c post transport:\n\n- `SiteHttpApi`, its posts group, and HTTP request envelopes;\n- generated-client type and service ownership without a handwritten client\n  interface;\n- handlers that delegate directly to `PostsService`;\n- browser Fetch and parameterized in-process client layers;\n- the server router layer and generated-client integration fixtures.\n\nIt reuses posts-owned schemas, branded `PostSlug`, projections, and tagged\nerrors. It must not import concrete posts Vite, Bun, Cloudflare, memory, or live\nlayers; app runtime composition supplies `PostsService`. It must not import or\nderive contracts from `@packages/rpc`. `SiteHttpApi` is public-read-only while\nthe app's successful-GET middleware is scoped to its entire router; private or\npersonalized groups require a separately composed cache boundary.\n\n## `@packages/rpc`\n\nRPC owns the retained compatibility transport:\n\n- `SiteRpcGroup`, its operation definitions, and RPC envelopes;\n- the typed client service, browser and in-process transports, handlers, and\n  test fixtures;\n- the `/rpc` HTTP layer composed by the app.\n\nRPC handlers delegate to the same published-only `PostsService` operations as\nthe HTTP API, but the transport definitions remain independent. Public post\nroute loaders use `@packages/http-api`; RPC remains mounted and verified as a\nseparate `no-store` contract.\n\n## `@packages/mcp`\n\nMCP owns the concrete public, read-only posts resource transport:\n\n- `SiteMcpHttp` and package-owned policy/URI/slug Schemas at the contract root;\n- `makeSiteMcpHttpLive(identity)` at `./live`, requiring `PostsService`;\n- the scoped memory-composed custom fetch at `./testing`; and\n- the private official SDK `McpServer.server` seam, Web Standard transport,\n  request Schemas, selected Cloudflare validator, resource encoding, HTTP\n  policy, and lifecycle. The selected validator, emitted production import /\n  constructor graph, and direct pinned-workerd execution together own the\n  Cloudfl