{"timestamp":"2026-09-23T23:37:32.847Z","ordinal":89996,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"019f3c64-2576-70c2-90c0-e6b212f79ee1","turn_id":"01a0d09d-47a5-7db3-b179-80b63f2ed88a","session_id":"019f3c64-2576-70c2-90c0-e6b212f79ee1","root_turn_id":"01a0d09d-47a5-7db3-b179-80b63f2ed88a","response_id":"resp_096c433c75860d41016ab462b637d481919def52bcdb5c4ded","usage":{"input_tokens":121285,"cached_input_tokens":119680,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":290,"reasoning_output_tokens":231,"total_tokens":121575},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5503586,"cached_input_tokens":5393792,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":9064,"reasoning_output_tokens":3266,"total_tokens":5512650},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":53965728,"cached_input_tokens":53092992,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":97670,"reasoning_output_tokens":42170,"total_tokens":54063398}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-23T23:37:32.890Z","ordinal":89997,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019f3c64-2576-70c2-90c0-e6b212f79ee1","turn_id":"01a0d09d-47a5-7db3-b179-80b63f2ed88a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-89c5466d-c2f0-4dd4-b826-96138f8274e1","process_id":"14929","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,180p' /Users/cooper/Projects/site/docs/architecture/cloudflare-alchemy-workers.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/Projects/bundjil","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,180p' /Users/cooper/Projects/site/docs/architecture/cloudflare-alchemy-workers.md","name":"cloudflare-alchemy-workers.md","path":"/Users/cooper/Projects/site/docs/architecture/cloudflare-alchemy-workers.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"---\ndocument_type: architecture\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: site-infrastructure-maintainer\nlast_reviewed: 2026-09-16\nreview_trigger: Alchemy stack, Cloudflare resource, route, observability, state, or provider-boundary change\n---\n\n# Cloudflare and Alchemy architecture\n\nThis document owns Site's current infrastructure model. Repository source says\nwhat should exist. Alchemy state, provider readback and public checks are\nseparate evidence of what actually exists and works.\n\nThe thin entrypoints are [`alchemy.run.ts`](../../alchemy.run.ts),\n[`alchemy.state.run.ts`](../../alchemy.state.run.ts) and\n[`alchemy.destroy.ts`](../../alchemy.destroy.ts). The deployment entrypoint\ndecodes a real `prod` or `pr-<number>` stage and declares resources. The\nstate-only entrypoint supplies the Cloudflare provider and same `Cloudflare.state()`\nwithout reading deployment inputs or declaring resources. The source-run\n[`@packages/infrastructure`](../../packages/infrastructure/README.md) package\nowns Cloudflare policy, observability planning, Axiom resources, dashboards,\nshared Schemas and site graph composition. Root and app callers use its\nexplicit exports; they do not import package internals by relative path. The\nexact Schema encoding and redaction step for the Cloudflare metrics secret is\nthe package-owned provider egress boundary.\n\n## Supported stages\n\nOnly two forms are supported:\n\n- `pr-<number>` for a pull-request Preview;\n- `prod` for Production.\n\nThe stage is Schema-decoded before the root graph is built. Any other value\nfails before resource declaration.\n\nBoth supported stages use one composed Cloudflare and Axiom provider Layer.\nThe Axiom layer supplies the HTTP service required while building the\nCloudflare layer. Alchemy then supplies provider credentials and the HTTP\nclient to resource operations and deploy-time Actions from that stack context.\nActions do not read provider credentials again from the process environment.\n\n```text\nalchemy.run.ts\n  -> Schema-decode stage and environment\n  -> @packages/infrastructure/stack: declareSiteStack\n  -> pr-<number>\n     -> Cloudflare Website\n     -> stage-owned Axiom ingest tokens\n     -> stage-owned Cloudflare trace and log destinations\n     -> shared account Secrets Store reference, stage-owned secret and Website binding\n     -> shared Production dataset names and endpoints\n     -> no Dataset, Dashboard, zone or Production route resources\n  -> prod\n     -> Cloudflare Website\n     -> retained zone\n     -> Website-owned apex and www custom-domain DNS/TLS\n     -> Website-owned www-to-apex redirect rule\n     -> three retained shared Axiom datasets\n     -> Production ingest tokens, destinations and metrics secret\n     -> six Production dashboards\n     -> six Preview-fleet dashboards\n```\n\n## Request runtime\n\nThe Website resource uses `main: \"src/worker.ts\"` under `apps/web` and\ncompatibility date `2026-07-28`, the minimum required by native tracing.\nAlchemy's public `makeWorkerBridge` runs the app's Effect Worker declaration;\nTanStack handles page rendering and routes inside it. The Alchemy build folds\n`globalThis.__ALCHEMY_RUNTIME__` to true, matching Alchemy's generated bundles.\nRuntime stack/stage metadata comes from Alchemy's existing environment bindings.\nThe generic Vite entry remains available for local development.\n\n`Cloudflare.Telemetry` owns native Effect spans. The Worker schedules lazy\nmetrics work with `WorkerExecutionContext.waitUntil`; no app-owned native\ntracer or importable-waitUntil adapter remains. See the\n[Effect service architecture](effect-services.md) for context propagation and\nsafe instrumentation. Local workerd `1.20260915.1` exercises this compatibility\ndate; hosted tracing still requires deployment and independent readback.\n\n## Resource inventory\n\nEvery provider mutation in the supported graph is declared through an\nAlchemy resource or Action. No workflow or command service creates, updates\nor deletes Cloudflare or Axiom resources directly.\n\n| Stage         | Alchemy declaration                           | Count | Desired/state owner  | Removal and foreign ownership                                   |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ----: | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `pr-<number>` | Cloudflare Website                            |     1 | exact Preview stage  | removed from exact saved stage                                  |\n| `pr-<number>` | Axiom ingest tokens                           |     2 | exact Preview stage  | removed from exact saved stage                                  |\n| `pr-<number>` | Cloudflare observability destinations         |     2 | exact Preview stage  | removed from exact saved stage                                  |\n| `pr-<number>` | Cloudflare Secrets Store reference and secret |     2 | exact Preview stage  | stage secret and state removed; shared physical store preserved |\n| `pr-<number>` | metrics-token qualification Action            |     1 | exact Preview stage  | bounded check, not a durable provider resource                  |\n| `pr-<number>` | shared Axiom datasets and dashboards          |     0 | `prod` only          | referenced by name and endpoint; never adopted by Preview       |\n| `prod`        | retained Axiom datasets                       |     3 | `prod`               | explicitly retained if removed from state                       |\n| `prod`        | Axiom ingest tokens                           |     2 | `prod`               | normal Alchemy lifecycle; Production authority required         |\n| `prod`        | Cloudflare observability destinations         |     2 | `prod`               | normal Alchemy lifecycle; Production authority required         |\n| `prod`        | Cloudflare Secrets Store reference and secret |     2 | `prod`               | stage secret lifecycle; shared physical store preserved         |\n| `prod`        | metrics-token qualification Action            |     1 | `prod`               | bounded check, not a durable provider resource                  |\n| `prod`        | Cloudflare Website                            |     1 | `prod`               | normal Alchemy lifecycle; Production authority required         |\n| `prod`        | Axiom dashboards                              |    12 | `prod`               | normal Alchemy lifecycle; Production authority required         |\n| `prod`        | adopted Cloudflare zone                       |     1 | `prod` state         | existing foreign zone is adopted and explicitly retained        |\n| `prod`        | Website custom domains and redirect           |     1 | nested Website shape | apex/www DNS, TLS and tagged redirect follow the Website        |\n| `prod`        | retained zone TLS settings                    |     2 | `prod`               | TLS 1.3 enabled and minimum TLS 1.3; retained on removal        |\n| `prod`        | retained zone DNSSEC                          |     1 | `prod`               | desired status active; retained on removal                      |\n\nThe Production graph therefore has 26 resource declarations plus one Action.\nA Preview has seven resource declarations plus one Action. Six resources are\nremoved by Preview cleanup; the seventh declaration references the account's\nshared default Secrets Store. The pinned Alchemy provider reuses that store\nand deliberately leaves it in place on deletion. Cleanup removes this stage's\nstore state entry and metrics secret, and preserves the physical store and all\nother secrets. The Cloudflare\naccount, domain registration, unrelated zone records, Doppler configs, GitHub\nEnvironments and old fixed-stage resources are outside this graph. The zone is\nadopted and retained; Alchemy must not delete it. The Website owns only the\napex and `www` custom-domain attachments, their Cloudflare-generated DNS/TLS,\nand the Alchemy-tagged `www` redirect rule. Alchemy state is the durable\ndeployment record, but direct provider and public checks remain separate\nevidence.\n\nThe repository audit found no Wrangler deployment path and no direct\nCloudflare or Axiom create, update or delete call outside the Alchemy graph.\nCustom post-deploy provider verification adapters have been removed. The empty-protobuf metrics request is the one\ndeclared Alchemy Action above and cannot create a durable resource.\n\n## Shared Axiom resources\n\nProduction is the only Alchemy owner of:\n\n- `site-prod-traces`;\n- `site-prod-logs`;\n- `site-prod-metrics`;\n- six Production dashboards;\n- six Preview-fleet dashboards.\n\nThe three Dataset Effects use Alchemy `retain()` so an ordinary state removal\ndoes not delete provider data. Intentional dataset deletion still needs exact\nprovider authority and independent readback.\n\nA Preview references the shared dataset names and OTLP endpoints. It does not\ndeclare or adopt the Dataset resources because Alchemy records resource\nownership by stack and stage. Declaring the same dataset from a Preview would\nbe cross-stage ownership, not harmless reuse.\n\nPreview-fleet dashboards are durable Production resources. Their queries\nrequire `environment=preview` and expose stage, Worker and revision. They help\noperators see the Preview fleet; they do not replace exact commit proof for\none pull request.\n\n### Request dashboards\n\nThe Overview and Routes & Performance definitions share the request query in\n`packages/infrastructure/src/axiom/dashboards/requests.ts`. They select HTTP\nserver spans, including requests with an upstream parent, rather than counting\ninternal Effect spans or all root spans. Their existing Alchemy resource\nidentities are preserved.\n\nOverview uses number cards for total, successful (2xx/3xx), bad (4xx), and\nfailed (5xx or a trace error) requests, plus P50/P95/P99 response times, outcome\ntrends and ranked path tables. Trace errors take precedence over status groups.\nOther outcomes remain included in the total. Routes & Performance adds a\nresponse-time heatmap, timing coverage, status trends, per-path percentiles,\nslow responses with trace IDs, and separate Worker execution percentiles.\nBoth dashboards provide an active path search filter. All Site dashboards\ndefault to seven days. Outcome cards use labelled green, orange and red themes;\ntiming cards remain neutral. Main response timings select successful GET requests\non the documented page paths (including post slugs), excluding redirects,\nmachine siblings and failed requests; bots can still request these pages.\nSelected-period P50/P95/P99 cards retain zeros and exclude missing values.\nThe hourly median/P95 chart reshapes percentile results into named series on a\nshared scale; its named legend table explicitly shows peak hourly values, not\nselected-period percentiles. Hourly request counts, timing\ncoverage and the zero-timing percentage expose sample size and clock limits.\n\nUser-agent panels group the recorded `attributes.user_agent.original` into\nreported crawler, reported script, browser-like, other and unknown categories.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"---\ndocument_type: architecture\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: site-infrastructure-maintainer\nlast_reviewed: 2026-09-16\nreview_trigger: Alchemy stack, Cloudflare resource, route, observability, state, or provider-boundary change\n---\n\n# Cloudflare and Alchemy architecture\n\nThis document owns Site's current infrastructure model. Repository source says\nwhat should exist. Alchemy state, provider readback and public checks are\nseparate evidence of what actually exists and works.\n\nThe thin entrypoints are [`alchemy.run.ts`](../../alchemy.run.ts),\n[`alchemy.state.run.ts`](../../alchemy.state.run.ts) and\n[`alchemy.destroy.ts`](../../alchemy.destroy.ts). The deployment entrypoint\ndecodes a real `prod` or `pr-<number>` stage and declares resources. The\nstate-only entrypoint supplies the Cloudflare provider and same `Cloudflare.state()`\nwithout reading deployment inputs or declaring resources. The source-run\n[`@packages/infrastructure`](../../packages/infrastructure/README.md) package\nowns Cloudflare policy, observability planning, Axiom resources, dashboards,\nshared Schemas and site graph composition. Root and app callers use its\nexplicit exports; they do not import package internals by relative path. The\nexact Schema encoding and redaction step for the Cloudflare metrics secret is\nthe package-owned provider egress boundary.\n\n## Supported stages\n\nOnly two forms are supported:\n\n- `pr-<number>` for a pull-request Preview;\n- `prod` for Production.\n\nThe stage is Schema-decoded before the root graph is built. Any other value\nfails before resource declaration.\n\nBoth supported stages use one composed Cloudflare and Axiom provider Layer.\nThe Axiom layer supplies the HTTP service required while building the\nCloudflare layer. Alchemy then supplies provider credentials and the HTTP\nclient to resource operations and deploy-time Actions from that stack context.\nActions do not read provider credentials again from the process environment.\n\n```text\nalchemy.run.ts\n  -> Schema-decode stage and environment\n  -> @packages/infrastructure/stack: declareSiteStack\n  -> pr-<number>\n     -> Cloudflare Website\n     -> stage-owned Axiom ingest tokens\n     -> stage-owned Cloudflare trace and log destinations\n     -> shared account Secrets Store reference, stage-owned secret and Website binding\n     -> shared Production dataset names and endpoints\n     -> no Dataset, Dashboard, zone or Production route resources\n  -> prod\n     -> Cloudflare Website\n     -> retained zone\n     -> Website-owned apex and www custom-domain DNS/TLS\n     -> Website-owned www-to-apex redirect rule\n     -> three retained shared Axiom datasets\n     -> Production ingest tokens, destinations and metrics secret\n     -> six Production dashboards\n     -> six Preview-fleet dashboards\n```\n\n## Request runtime\n\nThe Website resource uses `main: \"src/worker.ts\"` under `apps/web` and\ncompatibility date `2026-07-28`, the minimum required by native tracing.\nAlchemy's public `makeWorkerBridge` runs the app's Effect Worker declaration;\nTanStack handles page rendering and routes inside it. The Alchemy build folds\n`globalThis.__ALCHEMY_RUNTIME__` to true, matching Alchemy's generated bundles.\nRuntime stack/stage metadata comes from Alchemy's existing environment bindings.\nThe generic Vite entry remains available for local development.\n\n`Cloudflare.Telemetry` owns native Effect spans. The Worker schedules lazy\nmetrics work with `WorkerExecutionContext.waitUntil`; no app-owned native\ntracer or importable-waitUntil adapter remains. See the\n[Effect service architecture](effect-services.md) for context propagation and\nsafe instrumentation. Local workerd `1.20260915.1` exercises this compatibility\ndate; hosted tracing still requires deployment and independent readback.\n\n## Resource inventory\n\nEvery provider mutation in the supported graph is declared through an\nAlchemy resource or Action. No workflow or command service creates, updates\nor deletes Cloudflare or Axiom resources directly.\n\n| Stage         | Alchemy declaration                           | Count | Desired/state owner  | Removal and foreign ownership                                   |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ----: | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `pr-<number>` | Cloudflare Website                            |     1 | exact Preview stage  | removed from exact saved stage                                  |\n| `pr-<number>` | Axiom ingest tokens                           |     2 | exact Preview stage  | removed from exact saved stage                                  |\n| `pr-<number>` | Cloudflare observability destinations         |     2 | exact Preview stage  | removed from exact saved stage                                  |\n| `pr-<number>` | Cloudflare Secrets Store reference and secret |     2 | exact Preview stage  | stage secret and state removed; shared physical store preserved |\n| `pr-<number>` | metrics-token qualification Action            |     1 | exact Preview stage  | bounded check, not a durable provider resource                  |\n| `pr-<number>` | shared Axiom datasets and dashboards          |     0 | `prod` only          | referenced by name and endpoint; never adopted by Preview       |\n| `prod`        | retained Axiom datasets                       |     3 | `prod`               | explicitly retained if removed from state                       |\n| `prod`        | Axiom ingest tokens                           |     2 | `prod`               | normal Alchemy lifecycle; Production authority required         |\n| `prod`        | Cloudflare observability destinations         |     2 | `prod`               | normal Alchemy lifecycle; Production authority required         |\n| `prod`        | Cloudflare Secrets Store reference and secret |     2 | `prod`               | stage secret lifecycle; shared physical store preserved         |\n| `prod`        | metrics-token qualification Action            |     1 | `prod`               | bounded check, not a durable provider resource                  |\n| `prod`        | Cloudflare Website                            |     1 | `prod`               | normal Alchemy lifecycle; Production authority required         |\n| `prod`        | Axiom dashboards                              |    12 | `prod`               | normal Alchemy lifecycle; Production authority required         |\n| `prod`        | adopted Cloudflare zone                       |     1 | `prod` state         | existing foreign zone is adopted and explicitly retained        |\n| `prod`        | Website custom domains and redirect           |     1 | nested Website shape | apex/www DNS, TLS and tagged redirect follow the Website        |\n| `prod`        | retained zone TLS settings                    |     2 | `prod`               | TLS 1.3 enabled and minimum TLS 1.3; retained on removal        |\n| `prod`        | retained zone DNSSEC                          |     1 | `prod`               | desired status active; retained on removal                      |\n\nThe Production graph therefore has 26 resource declarations plus one Action.\nA Preview has seven resource declarations plus one Action. Six resources are\nremoved by Preview cleanup; the seventh declaration references the account's\nshared default Secrets Store. The pinned Alchemy provider reuses that store\nand deliberately leaves it in place on deletion. Cleanup removes this stage's\nstore state entry and metrics secret, and preserves the physical store and all\nother secrets. The Cloudflare\naccount, domain registration, unrelated zone records, Doppler configs, GitHub\nEnvironments and old fixed-stage resources are outside this graph. The zone is\nadopted and retained; Alchemy must not delete it. The Website owns only the\napex and `www` custom-domain attachments, their Cloudflare-generated DNS/TLS,\nand the Alchemy-tagged `www` redirect rule. Alchemy state is the durable\ndeployment record, but direct provider and public checks remain separate\nevidence.\n\nThe repository audit found no Wrangler deployment path and no direct\nCloudflare or Axiom create, update or delete call outside the Alchemy graph.\nCustom post-deploy provider verification adapters have been removed. The empty-protobuf metrics request is the one\ndeclared Alchemy Action above and cannot create a durable resource.\n\n## Shared Axiom resources\n\nProduction is the only Alchemy owner of:\n\n- `site-prod-traces`;\n- `site-prod-logs`;\n- `site-prod-metrics`;\n- six Production dashboards;\n- six Preview-fleet dashboards.\n\nThe three Dataset Effects use Alchemy `retain()` so an ordinary state removal\ndoes not delete provider data. Intentional dataset deletion still needs exact\nprovider authority and independent readback.\n\nA Preview references the shared dataset names and OTLP endpoints. It does not\ndeclare or adopt the Dataset resources because Alchemy records resource\nownership by stack and stage. Declaring the same dataset from a Preview would\nbe cross-stage ownership, not harmless reuse.\n\nPreview-fleet dashboards are durable Production resources. Their queries\nrequire `environment=preview` and expose stage, Worker and revision. They help\noperators see the Preview fleet; they do not replace exact commit proof for\none pull request.\n\n### Request dashboards\n\nThe Overview and Routes & Performance definitions share the request query in\n`packages/infrastructure/src/axiom/dashboards/requests.ts`. They select HTTP\nserver spans, including requests with an upstream parent, rather than counting\ninternal Effect spans or all root spans. Their existing Alchemy resource\nidentities are preserved.\n\nOverview uses number cards for total, successful (2xx/3xx), bad (4xx), and\nfailed (5xx or a trace error) requests, plus P50/P95/P99 response times, outcome\ntrends and ranked path tables. Trace errors take precedence over status groups.\nOther outcomes remain included in the total. Routes & Performance adds a\nresponse-time heatmap, timing coverage, status trends, per-path percentiles,\nslow responses with trace IDs, and separate Worker execution percentiles.\nBoth dashboards provide an active path search filter. All Site dashboards\ndefault to seven days. Outcome cards use labelled green, orange and red themes;\ntiming cards remain neutral. Main response timings select successful GET requests\non the documented page paths (including post slugs), excluding redirects,\nmachine siblings and failed requests; bots can still request these pages.\nSelected-period P50/P95/P99 cards retain zeros and exclude missing values.\nThe hourly median/P95 chart reshapes percentile results into named series on a\nshared scale; its named legend table explicitly shows peak hourly values, not\nselected-period percentiles. Hourly request counts, timing\ncoverage and the zero-timing percentage expose sample size and clock limits.\n\nUser-agent panels group the recorded `attributes.user_agent.original` into\nreported crawler, reported script, browser-like, other and unknown categories.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7792},"formatted_output":"---\ndocument_type: architecture\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: site-infrastructure-maintainer\nlast_reviewed: 2026-09-16\nreview_trigger: Alchemy stack, Cloudflare resource, route, observability, state, or provider-boundary change\n---\n\n# Cloudflare and Alchemy architecture\n\nThis document owns Site's current infrastructure model. Repository source says\nwhat should exist. Alchemy state, provider readback and public checks are\nseparate evidence of what actually exists and works.\n\nThe thin entrypoints are [`alchemy.run.ts`](../../alchemy.run.ts),\n[`alchemy.state.run.ts`](../../alchemy.state.run.ts) and\n[`alchemy.destroy.ts`](../../alchemy.destroy.ts). The deployment entrypoint\ndecodes a real `prod` or `pr-<number>` stage and declares resources. The\nstate-only entrypoint supplies the Cloudflare provider and same `Cloudflare.state()`\nwithout reading deployment inputs or declaring resources. The source-run\n[`@packages/infrastructure`](../../packages/infrastructure/README.md) package\nowns Cloudflare policy, observability planning, Axiom resources, dashboards,\nshared Schemas and site graph composition. Root and app callers use its\nexplicit exports; they do not import package internals by relative path. The\nexact Schema encoding and redaction step for the Cloudflare metrics secret is\nthe package-owned provider egress boundary.\n\n## Supported stages\n\nOnly two forms are supported:\n\n- `pr-<number>` for a pull-request Preview;\n- `prod` for Production.\n\nThe stage is Schema-decoded before the root graph is built. Any other value\nfails before resource declaration.\n\nBoth supported stages use one composed Cloudflare and Axiom provider Layer.\nThe Axiom layer supplies the HTTP service required while building the\nCloudflare layer. Alchemy then supplies provider credentials and the HTTP\nclient to resource operations and deploy-time Actions from that stack context.\nActions do not read provider credentials again from the process environment.\n\n```text\nalchemy.run.ts\n  -> Schema-decode stage and environment\n  -> @packages/infrastructure/stack: declareSiteStack\n  -> pr-<number>\n     -> Cloudflare Website\n     -> stage-owned Axiom ingest tokens\n     -> stage-owned Cloudflare trace and log destinations\n     -> shared account Secrets Store reference, stage-owned secret and Website binding\n     -> shared Production dataset names and endpoints\n     -> no Dataset, Dashboard, zone or Production route resources\n  -> prod\n     -> Cloudflare Website\n     -> retained zone\n     -> Website-owned apex and www custom-domain DNS/TLS\n     -> Website-owned www-to-apex redirect rule\n     -> three retained shared Axiom datasets\n     -> Production ingest tokens, destinations and metrics secret\n     -> six Production dashboards\n     -> six Preview-fleet dashboards\n```\n\n## Request runtime\n\nThe Website resource uses `main: \"src/worker.ts\"` under `apps/web` and\ncompatibility date `2026-07-28`, the minimum required by native tracing.\nAlchemy's public `makeWorkerBridge` runs the app's Effect Worker declaration;\nTanStack handles page rendering and routes inside it. The Alchemy build folds\n`globalThis.__ALCHEMY_RUNTIME__` to true, matching Alchemy's generated bundles.\nRuntime stack/stage metadata comes from Alchemy's existing environment bindings.\nThe generic Vite entry remains available for local development.\n\n`Cloudflare.Telemetry` owns native Effect spans. The Worker schedules lazy\nmetrics work with `WorkerExecutionContext.waitUntil`; no app-owned native\ntracer or importable-waitUntil adapter remains. See the\n[Effect service architecture](effect-services.md) for context propagation and\nsafe instrumentation. Local workerd `1.20260915.1` exercises this compatibility\ndate; hosted tracing still requires deployment and independent readback.\n\n## Resource inventory\n\nEvery provider mutation in the supported graph is declared through an\nAlchemy resource or Action. No workflow or command service creates, updates\nor deletes Cloudflare or Axiom resources directly.\n\n| Stage         | Alchemy declaration                           | Count | Desired/state owner  | Removal and foreign ownership                                   |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ----: | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `pr-<number>` | Cloudflare Website                            |     1 | exact Preview stage  | removed from exact saved stage                                  |\n| `pr-<number>` | Axiom ingest tokens                           |     2 | exact Preview stage  | removed from exact saved stage                                  |\n| `pr-<number>` | Cloudflare observability destinations         |     2 | exact Preview stage  | removed from exact saved stage                                  |\n| `pr-<number>` | Cloudflare Secrets Store reference and secret |     2 | exact Preview stage  | stage secret and state removed; shared physical store preserved |\n| `pr-<number>` | metrics-token qualification Action            |     1 | exact Preview stage  | bounded check, not a durable provider resource                  |\n| `pr-<number>` | shared Axiom datasets and dashboards          |     0 | `prod` only          | referenced by name and endpoint; never adopted by Preview       |\n| `prod`        | retained Axiom datasets                       |     3 | `prod`               | explicitly retained if removed from state                       |\n| `prod`        | Axiom ingest tokens                           |     2 | `prod`               | normal Alchemy lifecycle; Production authority required         |\n| `prod`        | Cloudflare observability destinations         |     2 | `prod`               | normal Alchemy lifecycle; Production authority required         |\n| `prod`        | Cloudflare Secrets Store reference and secret |     2 | `prod`               | stage secret lifecycle; shared physical store preserved         |\n| `prod`        | metrics-token qualification Action            |     1 | `prod`               | bounded check, not a durable provider resource                  |\n| `prod`        | Cloudflare Website                            |     1 | `prod`               | normal Alchemy lifecycle; Production authority required         |\n| `prod`        | Axiom dashboards                              |    12 | `prod`               | normal Alchemy lifecycle; Production authority required         |\n| `prod`        | adopted Cloudflare zone                       |     1 | `prod` state         | existing foreign zone is adopted and explicitly retained        |\n| `prod`        | Website custom domains and redirect           |     1 | nested Website shape | apex/www DNS, TLS and tagged redirect follow the Website        |\n| `prod`        | retained zone TLS settings                    |     2 | `prod`               | TLS 1.3 enabled and minimum TLS 1.3; retained on removal        |\n| `prod`        | retained zone DNSSEC                          |     1 | `prod`               | desired status active; retained on removal                      |\n\nThe Production graph therefore has 26 resource declarations plus one Action.\nA Preview has seven resource declarations plus one Action. Six resources are\nremoved by Preview cleanup; the seventh declaration references the account's\nshared default Secrets Store. The pinned Alchemy provider reuses that store\nand deliberately leaves it in place on deletion. Cleanup removes this stage's\nstore state entry and metrics secret, and preserves the physical store and all\nother secrets. The Cloudflare\naccount, domain registration, unrelated zone records, Doppler configs, GitHub\nEnvironments and old fixed-stage resources are outside this graph. The zone is\nadopted and retained; Alchemy must not delete it. The Website owns only the\napex and `www` custom-domain attachments, their Cloudflare-generated DNS/TLS,\nand the Alchemy-tagged `www` redirect rule. Alchemy state is the durable\ndeployment record, but direct provider and public checks remain separate\nevidence.\n\nThe repository audit found no Wrangler deployment path and no direct\nCloudflare or Axiom create, update or delete call outside the Alchemy graph.\nCustom post-deploy provider verification adapters have been removed. The empty-protobuf metrics request is the one\ndeclared Alchemy Action above and cannot create a durable resource.\n\n## Shared Axiom resources\n\nProduction is the only Alchemy owner of:\n\n- `site-prod-traces`;\n- `site-prod-logs`;\n- `site-prod-metrics`;\n- six Production dashboards;\n- six Preview-fleet dashboards.\n\nThe three Dataset Effects use Alchemy `retain()` so an ordinary state removal\ndoes not delete provider data. Intentional dataset deletion still needs exact\nprovider authority and independent readback.\n\nA Preview references the shared dataset names and OTLP endpoints. It does not\ndeclare or adopt the Dataset resources because Alchemy records resource\nownership by stack and stage. Declaring the same dataset from a Preview would\nbe cross-stage ownership, not harmless reuse.\n\nPreview-fleet dashboards are durable Production resources. Their queries\nrequire `environment=preview` and expose stage, Worker and revision. They help\noperators see the Preview fleet; they do not replace exact commit proof for\none pull request.\n\n### Request dashboards\n\nThe Overview and Routes & Performance definitions share the request query in\n`packages/infrastructure/src/axiom/dashboards/requests.ts`. They select HTTP\nserver spans, including requests with an upstream parent, rather than counting\ninternal Effect spans or all root spans. Their existing Alchemy resource\nidentities are preserved.\n\nOverview uses number cards for total, successful (2xx/3xx), bad (4xx), and\nfailed (5xx or a trace error) requests, plus P50/P95/P99 response times, outcome\ntrends and ranked path tables. Trace errors take precedence over status groups.\nOther outcomes remain included in the total. Routes & Performance adds a\nresponse-time heatmap, timing coverage, status trends, per-path percentiles,\nslow responses with trace IDs, and separate Worker execution percentiles.\nBoth dashboards provide an active path search filter. All Site dashboards\ndefault to seven days. Outcome cards use labelled green, orange and red themes;\ntiming cards remain neutral. Main response timings select successful GET requests\non the documented page paths (including post slugs), excluding redirects,\nmachine siblings and failed requests; bots can still request these pages.\nSelected-period P50/P95/P99 cards retain zeros and exclude missing values.\nThe hourly median/P95 chart reshapes percentile results into named series on a\nshared scale; its named legend table explicitly shows peak hourly values, not\nselected-period percentiles. Hourly request counts, timing\ncoverage and the zero-timing percentage expose sample size and clock limits.\n\nUser-agent panels group the recorded `attributes.user_agent.original` into\nreported crawler, reported script, browser-like, other and unknown categories.\n"},"started_at_ms":1790206652890,"completed_at_ms":1790206652890}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-23T23:37:32.895Z","ordinal":89998,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0d0a1-b1df-7343-93bb-3aa24c8658ec","call_id":"call_00ePFvqk0xQlHITPrhXYkJVh","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2756)\nTotal output lines: 180\n\n---\ndocument_type: architecture\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: site-infrastructure-maintainer\nlast_reviewed: 2026-09-16\nreview_trigger: Alchemy stack, Cloudflare resource, route, observability, state, or provider-boundary change\n---\n\n# Cloudflare and Alchemy architecture\n\nThis document owns Site's current infrastructure model. Repository source says\nwhat should exist. Alchemy state, provider readback and public checks are\nseparate evidence of what actually exists and works.\n\nThe thin entrypoints are [`alchemy.run.ts`](../../alchemy.run.ts),\n[`alchemy.state.run.ts`](../../alchemy.state.run.ts) and\n[`alchemy.destroy.ts`](../../alchemy.destroy.ts). The deployment entrypoint\ndecodes a real `prod` or `pr-<number>` stage and declares resources. The\nstate-only entrypoint supplies the Cloudflare provider and same `Cloudflare.state()`\nwithout reading deployment inputs or declaring resources. The source-run\n[`@packages/infrastructure`](../../packages/infrastructure/README.md) package\nowns Cloudflare policy, observability planning, Axiom resources, dashboards,\nshared Schemas and site graph composition. Root and app callers use its\nexplicit exports; they do not import package internals by relative path. The\nexact Schema encoding and redaction step for the Cloudflare metrics secret is\nthe package-owned provider egress boundary.\n\n## Supported stages\n\nOnly two forms are supported:\n\n- `pr-<number>` for a pull-request Preview;\n- `prod` for Production.\n\nThe stage is Schema-decoded before the root graph is built. Any other value\nfails before resource declaration.\n\nBoth supported stages use one composed Cloudflare and Axiom provider Layer.\nThe Axiom layer supplies the HTTP service required while building the\nCloudflare layer. Alchemy then supplies provider credentials and the HTTP\nclient to resource operations and deploy-time Actions from that stack context.\nActions do not read provider credentials again from the process environment.\n\n```text\nalchemy.run.ts\n  -> Schema-decode stage and environment\n  -> @packages/infrastructure/stack: declareSiteStack\n  -> pr-<number>\n     -> Cloudflare Website\n     -> stage-owned Axiom ingest tokens\n     -> stage-owned Cloudflare trace and log destinations\n     -> shared account Secrets Store reference, stage-owned secret and Website binding\n     -> shared Production dataset names and endpoints\n     -> no Dataset, Dashboard, zone or Production route resources\n  -> prod\n     -> Cloudflare Website\n     -> retained zone\n     -> Website-owned apex and www custom-domain DNS/TLS\n     -> Website-owned www-to-apex redirect rule\n     -> three retained shared Axiom datasets\n     -> Production ingest tokens, destinations and metrics secret\n     -> six Production dashboards\n     -> six Preview-fleet dashboards\n```\n\n## Request runtime\n\nThe Website resource uses `main: \"src/worker.ts\"` under `apps/web` and\ncompatibility date `2026-07-28`, the minimum required by native tracing.\nAlchemy's public `makeWorkerBridge` runs the app's Effect Worker declaration;\nTanStack handles page rendering and routes inside it. The Alchemy build folds\n`globalThis.__ALCHEMY_RUNTIME__` to true, matching Alchemy's generated bundles.\nRuntime stack/stage metadata comes from Alchemy's existing environment bindings.\nThe generic Vite entry remains available for local development.\n\n`Cloudflare.Telemetry` owns native Effect spans. The Worker schedules lazy\nmetrics work with `WorkerExecutionContext.waitUntil`; no app-owned native\ntracer or importable-waitUntil adapter remains. See the\n[Effect service architecture](effect-services.md) for context propagation and\nsafe instrumentation. Local workerd `1.20260915.1` exercises this compatibility\ndate; hosted tracing still requires deployment and independent readback.\n\n## Resource inventory\n\nEvery provider mutation in the supported graph is declared through an\nAlchemy resource or Action. No workflow or command service creates, updates\nor deletes Cloudflare or Axiom resources directly.\n\n| Stage         | Alchemy declaration                           | Count | Desired/state owner  | Removal and foreign ownership                                   |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ----: | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `pr-<number>` | Cloudflare Website                            |     1 | exact Preview stage  | removed from exact saved stage                                  |\n| `pr-<number>` | Axiom ingest tokens                           |     2 | exact Preview stage  | removed from exact saved stage                                  |\n| `pr-<number>` | Cloudflare observability destinations         |     2 | exact Preview stage  | removed from exact saved stage                                  |\n| `pr-<number>` | Cloudflare Secrets Store reference and secret |     2 | exact Preview stage  | stage secret and state removed; shared physical store preserved |\n| `pr-<number>` | metrics-token qualification Action            |     1 | exact Preview stage  | bounded check, not a durable provider resource                  |\n| `pr-<number>` | shared Axiom datasets and dashboards          |     0 …156 tokens truncated…e reference and secret |     2 | `prod`               | stage secret lifecycle; shared physical store preserved         |\n| `prod`        | metrics-token qualification Action            |     1 | `prod`               | bounded check, not a durable provider resource                  |\n| `prod`        | Cloudflare Website                            |     1 | `prod`               | normal Alchemy lifecycle; Production authority required         |\n| `prod`        | Axiom dashboards                              |    12 | `prod`               | normal Alchemy lifecycle; Production authority required         |\n| `prod`        | adopted Cloudflare zone                       |     1 | `prod` state         | existing foreign zone is adopted and explicitly retained        |\n| `prod`        | Website custom domains and redirect           |     1 | nested Website shape | apex/www DNS, TLS and tagged redirect follow the Website        |\n| `prod`        | retained zone TLS settings                    |     2 | `prod`               | TLS 1.3 enabled and minimum TLS 1.3; retained on removal        |\n| `prod`        | retained zone DNSSEC                          |     1 | `prod`               | desired status active; retained on removal                      |\n\nThe Production graph therefore has 26 resource declarations plus one Action.\nA Preview has seven resource declarations plus one Action. Six resources are\nremoved by Preview cleanup; the seventh declaration references the account's\nshared default Secrets Store. The pinned Alchemy provider reuses that store\nand deliberately leaves it in place on deletion. Cleanup removes this stage's\nstore state entry and metrics secret, and preserves the physical store and all\nother secrets. The Cloudflare\naccount, domain registration, unrelated zone records, Doppler configs, GitHub\nEnvironments and old fixed-stage resources are outside this graph. The zone is\nadopted and retained; Alchemy must not delete it. The Website owns only the\napex and `www` custom-domain attachments, their Cloudflare-generated DNS/TLS,\nand the Alchemy-tagged `www` redirect rule. Alchemy state is the durable\ndeployment record, but direct provider and public checks remain separate\nevidence.\n\nThe repository audit found no Wrangler deployment path and no direct\nCloudflare or Axiom create, update or delete call outside the Alchemy graph.\nCustom post-deploy provider verification adapters have been removed. The empty-protobuf metrics request is the one\ndeclared Alchemy Action above and cannot create a durable resource.\n\n## Shared Axiom resources\n\nProduction is the only Alchemy owner of:\n\n- `site-prod-traces`;\n- `site-prod-logs`;\n- `site-prod-metrics`;\n- six Production dashboards;\n- six Preview-fleet dashboards.\n\nThe three Dataset Effects use Alchemy `retain()` so an ordinary state removal\ndoes not delete provider data. Intentional dataset deletion still needs exact\nprovider authority and independent readback.\n\nA Preview references the shared dataset names and OTLP endpoints. It does not\ndeclare or adopt the Dataset resources because Alchemy records resource\nownership by stack and stage. Declaring the same dataset from a Preview would\nbe cross-stage ownership, not harmless reuse.\n\nPreview-fleet dashboards are durable Production resources. Their queries\nrequire `environment=preview` and expose stage, Worker and revision. They help\noperators see the Preview fleet; they do not replace exact commit proof for\none pull request.\n\n### Request dashboards\n\nThe Overview and Routes & Performance definitions share the request query in\n`packages/infrastructure/src/axiom/dashboards/requests.ts`. They select HTTP\nserver spans, including requests with an upstream parent, rather than counting\ninternal Effect spans or all root spans. Their existing Alchemy resource\nidentities are preserved.\n\nOverview uses number cards for total, successful (2xx/3xx), bad (4xx), and\nfailed (5xx or a trace error) requests, plus P50/P95/P99 response times, outcome\ntrends and ranked path tables. Trace errors take precedence over status groups.\nOther outcomes remain included in the total. Routes & Performance adds a\nresponse-time heatmap, timing coverage, status trends, per-path percentiles,\nslow responses with trace IDs, and separate Worker execution percentiles.\nBoth dashboards provide an active path search filter. All Site dashboards\ndefault to seven days. Outcome cards use labelled green, orange and red themes;\ntiming cards remain neutral. Main response timings select successful GET requests\non the documented page paths (including post slugs), excluding redirects,\nmachine siblings and failed requests; bots can still request these pages.\nSelected-period P50/P95/P99 cards retain zeros and exclude missing values.\nThe hourly median/P95 chart reshapes percentile results into named series on a\nshared scale; its named legend table explicitly shows peak hourly values, not\nselected-period percentiles. Hourly request counts, timing\ncoverage and the zero-timing percentage expose sample size and clock limits.\n\nUser-agent panels group the recorded `attributes.user_agent.original` into\nreported crawler, reported script, browser-like, other and unknown categories.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0d09d-47a5-7db3-b179-80b63f2ed88a","create_time":1790206652.895376}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
