{"timestamp":"2026-09-23T23:41:18.124Z","ordinal":90177,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019f3c64-2576-70c2-90c0-e6b212f79ee1","turn_id":"01a0d09d-47a5-7db3-b179-80b63f2ed88a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-25c0be1c-9542-493b-acaf-1a8da45485a9","process_id":"90927","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '176,196p' docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/Projects/bundjil","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '176,196p' docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md","name":"testing-and-quality.md","path":"docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"no workflow, deployment, provider, message, or Production authority.\n\n`bun run eval:hgi-307` is an opt-in check of the accepted historical epoch: all twelve\nfresh-context scenario receipts, the exact scenario-manifest digest, distinct\nfour-clock fields, intervention decisions, every docs/README path inventory,\nand the full docs/README/lint/skills/config/tests/CI/runbooks/rollback impact\nledger. Repository-local evaluated skills are read from the epoch's exact Git\nbase commit rather than the mutable working tree; external skill identities\nremain the epoch's stored digest receipts. Current skill behavior is owned by\nthe repository skill-policy checks and a separately qualified successor epoch.\nGitHub CI therefore checks out full repository history before running\nverification; a shallow checkout cannot supply the intentionally historical\nskill object and must not be treated as an evaluator failure or bypassed by\nweakening the epoch identity. Ordinary CI does not replay this dated receipt;\nit uses a shallow checkout and runs the current policy checks, lint, types,\nbuild, and behavior tests. Run the historical evaluator only with full Git\nhistory when explicitly reviewing that epoch.\n\nApp Vitest configurations that exercise workspace packages must select the\n`@bundjil/source` export condition and inline `@bundjil/*` for SSR resolution.\nThe source condition alone is insufficient when Vitest externalises the\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"no workflow, deployment, provider, message, or Production authority.\n\n`bun run eval:hgi-307` is an opt-in check of the accepted historical epoch: all twelve\nfresh-context scenario receipts, the exact scenario-manifest digest, distinct\nfour-clock fields, intervention decisions, every docs/README path inventory,\nand the full docs/README/lint/skills/config/tests/CI/runbooks/rollback impact\nledger. Repository-local evaluated skills are read from the epoch's exact Git\nbase commit rather than the mutable working tree; external skill identities\nremain the epoch's stored digest receipts. Current skill behavior is owned by\nthe repository skill-policy checks and a separately qualified successor epoch.\nGitHub CI therefore checks out full repository history before running\nverification; a shallow checkout cannot supply the intentionally historical\nskill object and must not be treated as an evaluator failure or bypassed by\nweakening the epoch identity. Ordinary CI does not replay this dated receipt;\nit uses a shallow checkout and runs the current policy checks, lint, types,\nbuild, and behavior tests. Run the historical evaluator only with full Git\nhistory when explicitly reviewing that epoch.\n\nApp Vitest configurations that exercise workspace packages must select the\n`@bundjil/source` export condition and inline `@bundjil/*` for SSR resolution.\nThe source condition alone is insufficient when Vitest externalises the\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":10417},"formatted_output":"no workflow, deployment, provider, message, or Production authority.\n\n`bun run eval:hgi-307` is an opt-in check of the accepted historical epoch: all twelve\nfresh-context scenario receipts, the exact scenario-manifest digest, distinct\nfour-clock fields, intervention decisions, every docs/README path inventory,\nand the full docs/README/lint/skills/config/tests/CI/runbooks/rollback impact\nledger. Repository-local evaluated skills are read from the epoch's exact Git\nbase commit rather than the mutable working tree; external skill identities\nremain the epoch's stored digest receipts. Current skill behavior is owned by\nthe repository skill-policy checks and a separately qualified successor epoch.\nGitHub CI therefore checks out full repository history before running\nverification; a shallow checkout cannot supply the intentionally historical\nskill object and must not be treated as an evaluator failure or bypassed by\nweakening the epoch identity. Ordinary CI does not replay this dated receipt;\nit uses a shallow checkout and runs the current policy checks, lint, types,\nbuild, and behavior tests. Run the historical evaluator only with full Git\nhistory when explicitly reviewing that epoch.\n\nApp Vitest configurations that exercise workspace packages must select the\n`@bundjil/source` export condition and inline `@bundjil/*` for SSR resolution.\nThe source condition alone is insufficient when Vitest externalises the\n"},"started_at_ms":1790206878124,"completed_at_ms":1790206878124}}
